## Types

```mdl
type Slide.takes
  desc: >
    Fields plugin-presenter's `Slide` holds for the recorder. A take is a plugin-studio `Variant` owned by the slide;
    its recorded `File` is owned by the take.
  fields:
    takes?: Ref<Variant>[]            # oldest first
    mainTake?: Ref<Variant>           # the take used when the voice-over plays or is exported
```

```mdl
type Take.Log
  desc: How a take was recorded, held in its Variant's `config`. Times are seconds from the start of the take.
  fields:
    duration: number
    steps: { step, at }[]             # click steps revealed while the slide was read
    device?: string                   # microphone label
    source: none | screen | camera
    session?: string                  # shared by the takes of one recording across the presentation
```

```mdl
type RecorderSettings
  fields:
    audioInput?: string               # microphone deviceId; unset prefers a /shure/i device, else the first
    videoSource?: none | screen | camera
    videoInput?: string               # camera deviceId
```

## Operations

```mdl
op DeleteTake
  key: org.dxos.operation.recorder.deleteTake
  desc: Deletes a take of a slide (and its file); the newest remaining take becomes main if it was. Undone by RestoreTake.
  input: { slide: Slide, take: Variant }
  output: { slide, take, index: number, main: boolean }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op RestoreTake
  key: org.dxos.operation.recorder.restoreTake
  desc: Re-adds a deleted take and its file at its place among the slide's takes, and its main mark.
  input: { slide, take, index: number, main: boolean }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op SelectTake
  key: org.dxos.operation.recorder.selectTake
  desc: Marks a take as its slide's main take.
  input: { slide: Slide, take: Variant }
  effects: [echo:write]
```

## Components

```mdl
component RecordButton
  desc: >
    The presenter toolbar item (PresenterSurface.Toolbar): records the whole presentation. Inside its click it creates
    the AudioContext and opens the microphone (processing off) and the screen or camera when set, then presents the
    deck from its first slide. Disabled while a recording starts or runs; shows why the last start failed.
  props: { subject: Presentation }
```

```mdl
component RecordingOverlay
  desc: >
    Over a deck being recorded (PresenterSurface.Overlay): the 3-2-1 count-in, then, centered at the top, REC, the
    recording's length, the time left on the slide when it has a desired length (red once over), and a compact level
    meter that shows a readout only to warn (NO SIGNAL, CLIP).
  props: { subject: Presentation }
```

```mdl
component LevelMeter
  desc: >
    Peak meter over -60..0 dBFS: the target band -12..-3 marked, a peak-hold marker for 1.5s, CLIP above -1 dBFS,
    and NO SIGNAL after 2s of digital silence.
  props: { peakDb?, holdDb?, rmsDb?, silent?, clip?, compact? }
```

```mdl
component RecordingsPanel
  desc: >
    The layout both Recordings companions share: the toolbar, a full-width RecordingList (a react-ui-list Listbox with
    shared column tracks, its leading check and trailing buttons under the toolbar's icons; the current row is the
    selection: a click or the arrow keys move it, Space plays or stops it, a double-click opens it), and the current
    row's player docked in the status bar, with no download menu.
  props: { toolbar, statusbar, children }
```

```mdl
component SlideRecordingsArticle
  desc: >
    The Recordings companion of a Slide, on RecordingsPanel. The toolbar records a new take of the slide (the deck
    presents from it; the recording ends when the reader leaves it), and saves an unsaved take again. The takes are a
    list with columns, newest first, unsaved ones first: an icon, the date and time it was recorded, its length, the
    slide's desired length, then a circle that a green check circle fills on the main take (it makes a take main), Play (in the status bar) and
    Delete (undoable; it discards an unsaved take).
  props: { slide: Slide }
```

```mdl
component PresentationRecordingsArticle
  desc: >
    The Recordings companion of a Presentation, on RecordingsPanel. The toolbar records every slide (a take per
    slide), plays every main take in order, and downloads them as one WAV. The presented slides are a list with
    columns: a circle (a green check circle when the slide has a main take), the title, take count, main take's length, desired
    length, then Play (its main take); a double-click opens the slide.
  props: { presentation: Presentation }
```

```mdl
component RecorderSettings
  desc: The plugin settings: microphone and camera pickers, the video source, and Test microphone with the meter.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Record
  req F-1.1: A Presentation's toolbar, and its Recordings companion's toolbar, record every slide, presenting the deck from its first slide.
  req F-1.2: A Slide's Recordings companion toolbar records that slide alone; the deck presents from it and the recording and presentation end when the reader leaves it.
  req F-1.3: Every recording starts with a 3-2-1 count-in shown over the deck; nothing is recorded during it.
  req F-1.4: The microphone is opened with echo cancellation, noise suppression and auto gain off.
  req F-1.5: A recording is split by slide: each slide read becomes a take of that slide, named by its start time; no take is overwritten.
  req F-1.6: A new take becomes its slide's main take.
  req F-1.7: A take that cannot be saved stays listed with Save again and Discard.
  req F-1.8: While recording, the deck shows REC, the recording's length and a level meter with NO SIGNAL and CLIP warnings, but no level readout, centered at the top.
  req F-1.9: While recording a slide with a desired length, the overlay shows the time left on it, and how far over once past.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Slide takes
  req F-2.1: A Slide has a Recordings companion listing its takes, newest first, with the main take marked.
  req F-2.2: A take's row has a check that makes it the main take, Play, and Delete; a delete can be undone.
  req F-2.4: Both Recordings companions share one layout: a toolbar, a keyboard-navigable list, and the current row's player in the status bar.
  req F-2.3: Each take shows its length against the slide's desired length, flagged when over.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Presentation voice-over
  req F-3.1: A Presentation has a Recordings companion listing each presented slide with its main take's length against its desired length.
  req F-3.2: A slide's row has Play (its main take) and a double-click opens the slide; Play all plays every main take in slide order.
  req F-3.3: Download saves the main takes, in slide order, as one WAV file.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Settings
  req F-4.1: The settings choose the microphone, the video source (none, screen, camera) and the camera.
  req F-4.2: Test microphone opens the chosen microphone on the level meter without recording.
  req F-4.3: With no microphone chosen, a device whose label matches /shure/i is preferred.
```

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: Record a presentation's voice-over, then re-record one slide
  desc: The primary journey — record every slide, re-record one, pick its main take, and download the voice-over.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-1.3, F-1.5, F-1.6, F-2.2, F-3.1, F-3.3]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - a Presentation named "QA Recording" with two slides, each with speaker notes; the first slide's Duration is 5
    - the Recorder plugin is enabled; video source None; a working microphone
  steps:
    - name: Record every slide
      do: Open "QA Recording" and press Record in its toolbar; allow the microphone. After 3-2-1, read slide 1, press →, read slide 2, press Escape.
      expect: the count-in shows, then REC; the presentation closes on Escape
      note: NO `invoke` — the recording must start inside a click (the media prompt and the AudioContext need it).
    - name: Check the voice-over
      do: Open the presentation's Recordings companion.
      expect: both slides list a main take; slide 1's is flagged over its 0:05
    - name: Re-record slide 1
      do: Open slide 1's Recordings companion and press Record; after 3-2-1 read it, then press →.
      expect: the presentation closes; slide 1 lists two takes, the new one marked Main
    - name: Choose the first read
      do: Press the check on the older take.
      expect: the older take is marked Main
    - name: Delete and undo
      do: Delete the newer take, then undo.
      expect: the take leaves the list, then returns
    - name: Download the voice-over
      do: In the presentation's Recordings companion press Download.
      expect: a WAV file named "QA Recording voice-over.wav" downloads
  after:
    - name: Delete the presentation
      do: Delete "QA Recording" (its slides own their takes).
      expect: the presentation and its takes are gone
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: A new plugin records a presentation's voice-over from a script, working with plugin-studio; a take is stored as a studio MediaArtifact.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Recording]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The plugin is named plugin-recorder; post-processing (trim, stretch, mux, loudness) runs on native ffmpeg, as an EDGE compute operation and as a desktop sidecar; video is a screen capture with a camera overlay, leaving room for other picture sources (autocue videos, canvas animations, presenter decks); plugin-presenter is the harness for the script.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [Recording, F-1]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: plugin-recorder adds a toolbar item to the presenter that starts the presentation and records its voice-over, and has settings to choose the microphone and the video source and to test the microphone.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordButton, RecorderSettings, F-1.1, F-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A Recording is parented to its Presentation and owns one MediaArtifact per kind (audio, video); each take is a Variant with its timeline in `config`, so no take type of its own exists. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Recording, Take.Log]
  why: Studio's Variant is already "one produced alternative with the request that made it"; a take is exactly that.
  rejected: A Take ECHO type beside Variant, which would duplicate studio's media model.
```

```mdl
decision D-5: A take's timeline is on the take's own clock, one section per slide visit keyed by Slide id, with click steps logged apart; recording starts with the presentation, with no hold before the first slide. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Take.Log, F-1.3]
  why: A deck has no picture timeline of its own, and ids survive slide reorders where positions do not.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The recorder is a capability service rather than state in the toolbar item, and follows the presentation through presenter's PresentationEventHandler. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordButton, F-1.3, F-1.4]
  why: The toolbar unmounts while the deck is presented; presenter must not depend on the recorder.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: A take that fails to save stays in memory with Save again and Save as a file; buffering it to IndexedDB is deferred. Takes are listed in a Recordings companion of the Presentation, not as navtree objects. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingsArticle, F-1.5, F-2.1]
  why: A take is the one thing the workflow must never lose; a companion keeps takes beside the deck they voice.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: Phase 1 records one video source (screen or camera); the camera overlay on a screen capture, post-processing, and other picture sources are later phases. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [F-1, RecorderSettings]
  why: Compositing the overlay needs a canvas pipeline; post-processing needs the EDGE and desktop runners.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: The Recordings companion has a toolbar, and each recording can be played, downloaded and deleted.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingsArticle, F-2.4, F-2.5]
```

```mdl
decision D-10: The recording panel and its meter are centered horizontally over the deck and show the time remaining on the slide when it has a desired length; the peak and level readout is not shown while recording.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingOverlay, LevelMeter, F-1.6, F-1.7]
```

```mdl
decision D-11: The overlay's compact meter still shows NO SIGNAL and CLIP, as warnings only; the companion plays a take with its own player rather than studio's VariantRenderer surface. Fills in [D-9] and [D-10].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [LevelMeter, RecordingsArticle]
  why: A muted microphone silently ruined two takes in the prototype; studio's surface renders only while plugin-studio is enabled.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Each slide has its own takes, held as an array on the Slide and shown in the slide's companion, whose toolbar records a new take. Takes can be played, deleted with undo, or selected as the main take. The presentation's companion records across all slides, splitting the recording by slide, and plays and downloads using each slide's preferred take. Supersedes [D-4] and [D-7].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  supersedes: D-4
  affects: [Slide.takes, SlideRecordingsArticle, PresentationRecordingsArticle, F-1, F-2, F-3]
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Every recording starts with a 3-2-1 count-in.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingOverlay, F-1.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-14: A recording runs one MediaRecorder per slide over the same input stream, so each slide read is a self-contained take; a new take becomes main; a one-slide recording ends, and closes the presentation, when the reader leaves its slide; the voice-over downloads as one WAV decoded from the main takes. Fills in [D-12].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [Take.Log, F-1.2, F-1.5, F-1.6, F-3.3]
  why: Compressed takes cannot be cut or joined in the browser without re-encoding; recording each slide separately needs no cut, and decoding to PCM is the one join the browser can do.
  rejected: One file per recording with per-slide time ranges, which needs a cut to download or replace one slide.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: Deleting a take is the DeleteTake operation, undone by RestoreTake through an undo mapping, which re-adds the take and its file at its place and restores its main mark. Fills in [D-12].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [DeleteTake, RestoreTake, F-2.2]
  why: The space's RemoveObjects unlinks only from collections, not from a slide's takes.
```

```mdl
decision D-16: The slide and presentation Recordings companions use one layout, built on react-ui-list (the standard current row, up and down, scrolling), with the player in the status bar at the bottom.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingsPanel, SlideRecordingsArticle, PresentationRecordingsArticle, F-2.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-17: The toolbar's actions act on the current row, rather than buttons on each row, and the status bar player reads a take's bytes into an object URL it owns. Fills in [D-16].
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingsPanel, F-2.2]
  why: A Listbox row is one navigable item; a URL shared through studio's cache was revoked under the player, which then showed 0:00 / 0:00.
```

```mdl
decision D-18: In both Recordings lists the current row is the selection.
  date: 2026-10-26
  by: user:richburdon
  affects: [RecordingsPanel, F-2.4]
```

